# Dependencies

| Tech | Use | Do NOT use |
|------|-----|------------|
| Redis | `ioredis` via `src/libs/redis.js` | node-redis, raw connections in controllers |
| Artemis/AMQP | `rhea` via `artemis.service.js` | amqplib unless matching existing pattern |
| JMS/STOMP | `ef-stompit` via `jms.service.js` | Custom STOMP clients |
| Vault | `node-vault` via `vault.config.js` | Hardcoded secrets |
| Real-time | `socket.io` via `socket.service.js` | — |
| HTTP clients | `axios` to CIM, conversation-manager, routing engine, etc. | — |

# Connection Architecture

- Redis, Artemis, JMS clients initialized in `src/index.js` bootstrap after Vault creds
- `VaultLeaseManager` / `vault.config.js` refreshes Redis and JMS credentials
- State: Redis + in-memory maps (`datastructure.manager.js`) — no MongoDB/ORM

# Redis

- Setup: `src/libs/redis.js`, operations: `src/services/redis.service.js`
- Sentinel/SSL support via config — do not create standalone Redis clients in services

# Artemis / JMS

- `artemis.service.js` — AMQP via rhea
- `jms.service.js`, `pullModeList.service.js` — STOMP via ef-stompit
- Follow existing publish/subscribe patterns; do not add parallel messaging stacks

# Socket.IO

- Attached in `src/index.js` after `app.listen()`
- Business logic in `socket.service.js` — not in route handlers

# Anti-patterns

- Do not create `new Redis()` or AMQP connections outside established service/libs modules
- Do not add Kafka, RabbitMQ, or alternate messaging unless platform team approves
